                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you play in Free-Read mode it is worth it.\nI would like to point out this version of Caverns of the Snow Witch is actually the extended play and has two parts.  The first half is the Snow Witch, the second half is.. grueling fluff to extend the story for a forced event that is hard-written to fail you so it can justify the second half of the story.  Yeah, don't even try to make sense of it.  That's what they did and all the cursing in the world won't change it.  Because of this, and how the author basically broke the game balance so badly that it became virtually impossible to beat, the only way you can complete the game is in Free Read mode.  Do NOT waste your time on normal and pfft. forget hard core.  If you are a glutton for death simulators, then go ahead but be aware that even if you start with flawless perfect stats, AND the RNG loves you all the way through, you still only have a 1 in 500 statistically calculated probability of ever reaching the end and getting the good ending.  1 in 500.  yup.  So, just think on that.  Then start your FREE-READ playthrough and just try to enjoy the story.",
